Rotator Cuff Tendinopathy — JOSPT, 2025 (@med-source-tendinopathy-guideline: 0, is #reference, #part-of @medicine-sources) { r_74MJTFK7YKMV06M2GFT8YZ5DFV
François Desmeules, Jean-Sébastien Roy, Simon Lafrance, and colleagues. Rotator Cuff Tendinopathy Diagnosis, Nonsurgical Medical Care, and Rehabilitation: A Clinical Practice Guideline. Journal of Orthopaedic & Sports Physical Therapy 55, 2025, pages 235–274. DOI: 10.2519/jospt.2025.13182. English.

[Authorized source](https://doi.org/10.2519/jospt.2025.13182).

Read the scope and definitions, then assessment, prognosis, nonsurgical care, rehabilitation, and return to activity. Its target includes tendinopathy with or without calcification and specified partial-thickness tears; full-thickness tears are outside its stated target. [APTA scope summary](https://www.apta.org/patient-care/evidence-based-practice-resources/cpgs/CPG_Rotator_Cuff_Tendinopathy_Diagnosis_Non-surgical_Medical_Care_Rehabilitation); [professional-association PDF](https://www.orthopt.org/uploads/content_files/files/Rotator_Cuff_CPG.pdf).

**Access and reuse:** Freely readable on the author, publisher, or institution website. Copyright remains with the stated rights holder; no local copy or permission to adapt is supplied.

